From 46d012c7dbca0e2341d8350ba97c6dbdabd6951d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:02:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(project): a typed hole floor no longer reads Stale after
 save and reopen

The Drill, Bore and Thread arms of the op stamp digest each hole (and
radial hole) through operation::hole_digest, which snaps every hole float
to the 1 um lattice the project file stores it on (HoleDto/CrossHoleDto).
A floor typed as 3.8099999999999996 mm and the 3.81 the file reloads now
stamp alike, so an op saved Ok reopens Ok. On-lattice holes hash exactly
as before; half a micron or more still moves the stamp. Same remedy as
#1351's path signature. Decision in docs/decisions/1560-hole-digest-lattice.md.

Fixes #1560

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
